# cm_script_docs_sync.baseline — CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC finding SET (§11.4.18, BOB-242)
#
# One key per line: NODOC:<path> (no docs/scripts/<name>.md) or
# DOCBEHIND:<path> (the script changed after its guide). Lines starting with '#'
# and blank lines are ignored. MONOTONE-DECREASING RATCHET (§11.4.135(5) /
# §11.4.224(E)):
#   * a finding NOT listed here FAILs the gate (NEW) — never add a row to hide one;
#   * a row whose finding no longer exists FAILs the gate (RETIRED) — delete the
#     row in the SAME change that writes or updates the guide.
# Compared by SET, not count, so a one-out-one-in swap is caught.
#
# Seeded 2026-09-26 from `check_cm_script_docs_sync.sh . --list` on the real
# tree at HEAD d36899a: 52 NODOC + 11 DOCBEHIND = 63 rows. Two findings the
# list printed were deliberately NOT seeded because they were transient working-
# tree state, not debt: the gate's own new script (its guide lands with it) and
# scripts/zero_shortcomings_audit.sh (uncommitted edits by a concurrent stream;
# its committed script and guide are in sync).
#
# Adoption choice: ratchet snapshot, the repository's established default for
# set-based gates. Open to an operator decision (§11.4.66) to switch to a hard
# floor or to changed-files-only enforcement.
DOCBEHIND:scripts/hooks/unattributed-commit-guard.sh
